# Data layer

- FalkorDB access: `server/graph.ts` (`GraphStore.read`, `GraphStore.write` = one `MULTI/EXEC`). Cypher helpers: `server/cypher.ts`.
- Repository: `server/repository.ts` (`GraphRepo`). Writes are serialized; each loads the workspace, validates (Zod, metamodel, existence, cycles), then writes. Never write before validation passes — Redis does not roll back.
- One graph per workspace, pointed to by `(:Workspace {graph})` in `lattice:meta`. Replace-import builds a new graph, then swaps the pointer.
- `parentId` / `ownerId` are derived from `CONTAINS` / `OWNED_BY` edges on read. Do not store them as properties.
- Type-specific component fields are plain node properties; anything on the Zod schema round-trips. Page `doc` and diagram `query`/`view` are JSON strings.
- Labels and relationship types come only from Zod enums (`componentLabel`, `relType`). Values always go through `$params`.
- Import remaps all IDs (`server/bundle.ts` `remapBundle`). Pages: `remapMentionIds`. Diagrams: `stripDanglingDiagramNodes`.
- Seed: `src/data/seed.ts`. Northstar must `bundleSchema.safeParse` and `integrityErrors(bundle) === []` (`src/lib/integrity.ts`).
- API: `server/app.ts`. Every response is a `Result<T>`; the URL decides `workspaceId`.
- Store: actions are async. Updates patch the local graph at call time, writes are queued, and the store reloads when the queue drains. Use `toastErrors` in UI.
